#
# Enable the SCST boot-time helpers on the StarlingX image.
#
# StarlingX ships 99-default-disable.preset (disable everything not explicitly
# enabled), so a unit's [Install] WantedBy and the package postinst's
# deb-systemd-helper enable do not take effect on the built image - the preset
# policy wins and the units come up disabled. Without these enabled at boot:
#   - scst-ctl-dev never creates /dev/iscsi-scst-ctl, so the gateway's
#     device-plugin DaemonSet fails to mount it and the gateway pod cannot
#     schedule (Insufficient starlingx.io/scst-iscsi-ctl).
# SCST module presence is not reported from here: node-feature-discovery
# publishes the loaded modules in its per-node NodeFeature object, and the
# rook-ceph app's pre-apply check reads them from there - no boot-time unit or
# node label is needed for that.
#
# A numeric prefix below 99 so it is evaluated before 99-default-disable.
enable scst-ctl-dev.service
